# Nisbat Home needs no API keys for the MVP.
#
# All external services used are public and key-free, and are called from
# Next.js route handlers on the server (src/app/api/*):
#   - AlQuran Cloud API (Quran text, translations, verse audio)  https://alquran.cloud/api
#   - Publisher RSS feeds (Sixty, Dawn, The Express Tribune, Al Jazeera, BBC Urdu)
#   - Open-Meteo (weather + geocoding)                           https://open-meteo.com
#   - AlAdhan (prayer times)                                     https://aladhan.com/prayer-times-api
#   - iptv-org community playlist (opt-in)                       https://github.com/iptv-org/iptv
#   - Open-Meteo Air Quality, hisnmuslim.com (adhkar), fawazahmed0/hadith-api,
#     iTunes Search + podcast RSS, YouTube channel RSS, Radio Pakistan,
#     Wikipedia "On this day"
#
# Optional: official State Bank of Pakistan exchange rates via PakDataHub
# (free key at https://pakdatahub.com — 500 calls/month is enough; Nisbat
# uses ~100). Without it, Bazaar shows an open reference rate, labelled.
# PAKDATAHUB_API_KEY=
#   - PBS weekly SPI prices are read from pbs.gov.pk directly (no key).
#
# Where the family-sync store and uploaded photos are kept (default ./data).
# NISBAT_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/nisbat
#
# If you later move to a keyed provider (e.g. the Quran Foundation API, which
# requires OAuth client credentials), add server-only variables here WITHOUT the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix so they never reach the browser bundle, for example:
# QURAN_CLIENT_ID=
# QURAN_CLIENT_SECRET=
